{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-94485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the elliptic cone $\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{8}=\\frac{(z+6)^{2}}{6},$ find its intercepts with the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $y$-intercepts of the elliptic cone, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-6)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{8} & =\\frac{(0+6)^{2}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{36}{9}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{8} & =\\frac{36}{6} \\\\ 4+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{8} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{8} & =2 \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =16 \\\\ y-4 & =\\pm 4 \\\\ y & =4\\pm 4 \\\\ y & =0,8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,0,0)$ and $(0,8,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1a73bd7aada661056a293c06bcd4a8c8096d4aca56f02c596e803474aee13e03"} {"question" "q-94485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,8,0)$"] ["text" "$(0,0,0)$ only"] ["text" "$(0,2,0)$ and $(0,8,0)$"] ["text" "$(0,4,0)$ and $(0,16,0)$"] ["text" "$(0,4,0)$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,8,0)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the elliptic cone $(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=(z-1)^{2}\\,?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{6} & =(z-1)^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =(z-1)^{2} \\\\ \\pm (x+1) & =z-1 \\\\ z & =\\pm (x+1)+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $xz$-plane with equations $z=-x$ and $z=x+2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1a73bd7aada661056a293c06bcd4a8c8096d4aca56f02c596e803474aee13e03"} {"question" "q-94490" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94490" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=-x"] ["math" "z=\\pm x+1"] ["math" "z=\\pm x-2"] ["text" "$z=-x,\\,$ $z=x+2$"] ["text" "$z=-x-2,\\,$ $z=-x$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94490" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$z=-x,\\,$ $z=x+2$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94605" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the elliptic cone $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}={z}^{2},$ find its intercept with the $z$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94605" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $z$-intercept of the elliptic cone, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation and solve for $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{9} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ 0+0 & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =0 \\\\ z & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercept with the $z$-axis is $(0,0,0)$ only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94605" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1a73bd7aada661056a293c06bcd4a8c8096d4aca56f02c596e803474aee13e03"} {"question" "q-94605" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94605" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,0,3)$"] ["text" "$(0,0,0)$ only"] ["text" "$(0,0,1)$ and $(0,0,9)$"] ["text" "$(0,0,1)$ only"] ["text" "$(0,0,3)$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94605" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(0,0,0)$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the center of the elliptic cone $9(x+3)^{2}+4(y+2)^{2}={z}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general equation of an elliptic cone with center at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=\\frac{(z-{z}_{0})^{2}}{{c}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo find the center, we rewrite our equation in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(x+3)^{2}+4(y+2)^{2} & =(z-0)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{1/9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{1/4} & =(z-0)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-3))^{2}}{1/9}+\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{1/4} & =(z-0)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an elliptic cone that has its center at $(-3,-2,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1a73bd7aada661056a293c06bcd4a8c8096d4aca56f02c596e803474aee13e03"} {"question" "q-94698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-3,-2,0)"] ["math" "(-9,-4,0)"] ["math" "(3,2,0)"] ["math" "(4,9,0)"] ["math" "(9,4,1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-94698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-3,-2,0)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-176835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the intersection of the elliptic cone $4(x+3)^{2}+8(y-1)^{2}=(z+7)^{2}$ and the plane $z=-3$ is an ellipse, what is the length of its major axis?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-176835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the intersection of the elliptic cone and the plane $z=-3,$ we substitute $z=-3$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x+3)^{2}+8(y-1)^{2} & =(-3+7)^{2} \\\\ 4(x+3)^{2}+8(y-1)^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ 4(x+3)^{2}+8(y-1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{(2)^{2}}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an ellipse with a semi-major axis of length $a=2.$ Therefore, the major axis has length $2a=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-176835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1a73bd7aada661056a293c06bcd4a8c8096d4aca56f02c596e803474aee13e03"} {"question" "q-176835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-176835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"} {"question" "q-176835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068740/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d7c6e80d8caac069dab40c79cca16ca4f59f3c2fccb83dc6427f54535be7826"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2317 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
